            {
                "entry_id": "7c8bc686-f12d-3731-849d-ae924cc50be3",
                "word": "boysenberry",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bd5177db-311c-4e5f-9197-55a411615dd4",
                        "entry_id": "7c8bc686-f12d-3731-849d-ae924cc50be3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "boysenberries"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8848397d-c487-36c1-abfd-e5221517d8bc",
                        "entry_id": "7c8bc686-f12d-3731-849d-ae924cc50be3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A hybrid berry created from crossing blackberry, red raspberry, and loganberry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60db8f79-dcf2-4f09-b107-3c2956d7d0fb",
                                "sense_id": "8848397d-c487-36c1-abfd-e5221517d8bc",
                                "text": "Like all caneberries, boysenberries are an etaerio or aggregate fruit containing several drupelets."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b21a54a-31d3-4f0f-be26-68bb6588785d",
                                "sense_id": "8848397d-c487-36c1-abfd-e5221517d8bc",
                                "text": "As mesmerizing as it is to watch Kristen Kish whip up bacon and cinnamon waffles with boysenberry and strawberry jam, imagine playing poker with Hosea Rosenberg."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "745acfb8-27c3-410c-aabb-405b3bc0d319",
                                "sense_id": "8848397d-c487-36c1-abfd-e5221517d8bc",
                                "text": "Here’s a grocery list of foods Chestnut has eaten competitively, drawn from his Major League Eating bio: apple pie, asparagus, boysenberry pie, brats, burritos, chicken spiedies (a kind of sandwich), chicken wings, chili, corned beef sandwiches, eggs, fish tacos, funnel cake, grilled cheese sandwiches, gyoza, Krystal hamburgers, horseshoe sandwiches, hot dogs, ice cream, jalapeno poppers, kolaches, pastrami sandwiches, Philly cheesesteaks, pierogi, pizza, pork ribs, pulled pork, poutine, salt potatoes, shrimp, tacos, tamales, turkey and Twinkies."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
